 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "mapping holds [phrase, category] pairs; a phrase is one or more alphanumeric words joined by single spaces. Scan review left to right. At a word start (an alphanumeric character at index 0 or after a non-alphanumeric one), take the longest phrase that matches the text there ignoring ASCII case and is followed by a non-alphanumeric character or the end; replace that text by \"[category]{text}\" keeping the original text, and continue after it. Otherwise copy one character. Case-insensitive matching, longest match, left-to-right non-overlapping replacement and \"first mapping wins\" for duplicate phrases are inferred.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
